WEBVTT

1
00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:42.668
SHOWBOX presents
a JOYRABBIT INC. Production

2
00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:05.148
CHOI Min-sik

3
00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:10.988
KIM Dong-hwi

4
00:01:57.868 --> 00:02:00.996
IN OUR PRIME

5
00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:38.324
The place where Korea's
top 1% gather.

6
00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:40.327
Oh, except me.

7
00:02:41.328 --> 00:02:43.872
I've been here for 213 days.

8
00:02:44.456 --> 00:02:46.792
I still feel out of place.

9
00:02:49.712 --> 00:02:52.505
No, it's only getting worse.

10
00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:57.510
Han Ji-woo, what are you doing?

11
00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:13.359
2V=4/3πr³.

12
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.445
Understand? Any questions?

13
00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:26.790
It's easy teaching
a group of geniuses,

14
00:03:27.374 --> 00:03:30.502
but I question myself
why I became a teacher.

15
00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.549
Even if you learned everything
from your tutors,

16
00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.261
shouldn't you still pretend
to ask me questions?

17
00:03:40.262 --> 00:03:41.888
Then I can pretend to answer.

18
00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:43.974
Then you go, "You're amazing!"

19
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:47.978
Isn't that what
a normal class looks like?

20
00:03:48.771 --> 00:03:49.772
All right.

21
00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:53.983
That's the entirety of
grade 12 curriculum

22
00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.693
even though you're in grade 10.

23
00:03:56.444 --> 00:03:58.362
You're making it too easy.

24
00:03:58.363 --> 00:03:59.947
No way!

25
00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:01.448
- No?
- Nope!

26
00:04:01.449 --> 00:04:02.910
- You sure?
- Yup!

27
00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.080
Right, we're not peasants.

28
00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:10.792
As a peasant, why am I here?

29
00:04:10.793 --> 00:04:12.419
Rank: 238 out of 240

30
00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.922
Math is especially problematic.

31
00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.758
You were flying high
in middle school, right?

32
00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.302
Yes.

33
00:04:20.803 --> 00:04:25.849
But if the math is this low,
there's no hope for you.

34
00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:29.061
Allow me to speak frankly.

35
00:04:29.812 --> 00:04:33.480
Even with middle tiers
at our school,

36
00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:35.566
Ivy League is a shoe-in.

37
00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:40.072
But with a tier 9 in crucial subjects,

38
00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:42.574
there's just no way.

39
00:04:44.659 --> 00:04:48.455
Heard about everyone going on
math bootcamps on weekends?

40
00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:50.372
Yes.

41
00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:55.670
You'd be in the top bracket
in a normal high school, right?

42
00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:02.760
I really hate to say it
as a teacher,

43
00:05:05.097 --> 00:05:06.431
but could you think it over?

44
00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:08.141
Pardon?

45
00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.602
Transferring out.

46
00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:15.815
Go home and discuss it
with your mom.

47
00:05:20.237 --> 00:05:21.403
So hungry...

48
00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:22.990
- Did you bring it?
- Of course.

49
00:05:29.579 --> 00:05:30.663
Hey, hey, hey!

50
00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:53.896
Huh?

51
00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.455
You sneaky punk.

52
00:06:17.752 --> 00:06:19.462
Stirred fried pork
and hard liquor...

53
00:06:20.047 --> 00:06:22.840
Pork and booze are
a fantastic combo.

54
00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:25.928
Who was it?

55
00:06:27.429 --> 00:06:28.180
What?

56
00:06:28.846 --> 00:06:30.640
I need a few names.

57
00:06:31.349 --> 00:06:32.517
Your 3 co-conspirators.

58
00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:35.019
There are none.

59
00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:38.105
4 sets of chopsticks,
and 4 spoons,

60
00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:40.107
you'll still stand your ground?

61
00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:41.150
Yes.

62
00:06:41.151 --> 00:06:42.485
Are you being rebellious?

63
00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:43.778
No.

64
00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.074
Okay, fine!

65
00:06:48.075 --> 00:06:51.077
Loyalty is important at your age.

66
00:06:51.078 --> 00:06:54.663
I was like that too
when I was in school.

67
00:06:54.664 --> 00:06:56.458
Of course I know.

68
00:06:57.292 --> 00:07:00.294
Ji-woo, look around.

69
00:07:00.295 --> 00:07:05.049
Your co-conspirators are only
looking out for themselves.

70
00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:09.846
You'll shed blood
for these cowards?

71
00:07:11.056 --> 00:07:12.474
Are you stupid?

72
00:07:14.392 --> 00:07:18.438
Spill it, or you'll be kicked out
of your dorm for a month.

73
00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:22.900
Now.

74
00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:26.487
I...

75
00:07:26.488 --> 00:07:27.239
Go on.

76
00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.285
I was going to eat it alone.

77
00:07:42.545 --> 00:07:46.132
Bud! You are a true friend,
how could I ever repay you?

78
00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.384
- It's fine.
- Oh yeah!

79
00:07:51.596 --> 00:07:52.389
What is it?

80
00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:55.141
Keep it, a gift of appreciation.

81
00:07:55.142 --> 00:07:58.352
Forget it, it's not necessary
between friends.

82
00:07:58.353 --> 00:07:59.437
Friends?

83
00:08:00.355 --> 00:08:01.772
Right, friends.

84
00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:04.401
Man, your mom will kill you, right?

85
00:08:05.152 --> 00:08:06.443
There is a way.

86
00:08:06.444 --> 00:08:08.987
Science building, B103.

87
00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:11.073
The legend has it,

88
00:08:11.074 --> 00:08:13.409
dorm rejects braved hardships

89
00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.494
and lived there until
they were led back in!

90
00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:17.413
We stayed here -
Yong-ho, Nam-hyuk, Seok-min

91
00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:19.248
It was turned into
storage long ago.

92
00:08:19.249 --> 00:08:20.792
So no one will find out...

93
00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:23.378
2 o'clock! Commie officer alert!

94
00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:28.883
Our delivery routes are
all blocked because of him!

95
00:08:29.384 --> 00:08:32.469
If we don't order late night snack,
who'll maintain local economy?

96
00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.138
When did he defect?

97
00:08:34.139 --> 00:08:37.308
It's been 4 years
since you defected.

98
00:08:37.309 --> 00:08:39.602
Please stop working
as a night guard.

99
00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.563
Just give me the pills.

100
00:08:42.564 --> 00:08:46.692
You're relying on sleeping pills
because your biorhythm is off...

101
00:08:46.693 --> 00:08:47.652
Then...

102
00:08:49.487 --> 00:08:51.864
you should find me a good job.

103
00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:53.574
Pardon?

104
00:08:53.575 --> 00:08:55.702
Prescribe me 20 days' worth.

105
00:08:57.079 --> 00:09:00.082
It ain't easy getting
time off to come here.

106
00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.192
Seoul Milk

107
00:09:33.281 --> 00:09:36.201
You punk, eat up.

108
00:09:38.745 --> 00:09:42.499
Why? Don't want to eat?

109
00:09:47.837 --> 00:09:49.756
Sample Questions

110
00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.923
This week's assignment.

111
00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:56.928
Even if you scour the internet,
you'll never find answers, why?

112
00:09:56.929 --> 00:09:59.516
These problems are from hell.

113
00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:11.153
Can I bum a cigarette?

114
00:10:15.698 --> 00:10:18.785
Alcohol is okay,
but not smokes?

115
00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.163
I don't drink.

116
00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:26.042
But you drink 4 bottles
of soju alone.

117
00:10:26.751 --> 00:10:27.960
Piss off.

118
00:10:31.298 --> 00:10:34.342
So cool, I almost fell for you.

119
00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.219
I thought you were
just a loser.

120
00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:38.095
What?

121
00:10:39.556 --> 00:10:43.059
Had you named names,
you all would've gotten a week.

122
00:10:44.561 --> 00:10:46.103
But look at you!

123
00:10:47.146 --> 00:10:49.482
You're not only a loser,
but dumb as hell.

124
00:10:56.072 --> 00:10:59.784
Hey, Han Ji-woo!
You watched too many movies!

125
00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.828
That's not friendship!

126
00:11:02.829 --> 00:11:03.746
Hey!

127
00:11:32.817 --> 00:11:34.610
Certificate of Commendation

128
00:11:34.611 --> 00:11:36.696
Certificate of Appointment

129
00:11:58.551 --> 00:11:59.344
Ji-woo!

130
00:12:00.094 --> 00:12:00.719
Mom.

131
00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:02.220
You didn't call ahead.

132
00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:06.057
Oh my, Ji-woo,
so good to see you!

133
00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:07.184
Are you drunk?

134
00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:08.686
Drunk?

135
00:12:10.855 --> 00:12:12.981
- Did you eat?
- Sort of.

136
00:12:12.982 --> 00:12:15.192
- You didn't?
- I ate, you?

137
00:12:15.902 --> 00:12:18.321
I had chicken and beer
with my colleagues.

138
00:12:18.946 --> 00:12:20.572
How's the new job?

139
00:12:20.573 --> 00:12:25.536
Yeah, bank call center is
much better than home shopping.

140
00:12:25.537 --> 00:12:27.747
No customers who swear at you?

141
00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.001
Come on, sit.

142
00:12:32.544 --> 00:12:33.545
Sit.

143
00:12:38.007 --> 00:12:39.967
How's school?
Is it fun?

144
00:12:40.718 --> 00:12:42.928
Yeah, it's fun.

145
00:12:42.929 --> 00:12:43.596
Good.

146
00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:51.938
You look so fancy in the uniform.

147
00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:55.983
Other moms are desperate
to have their kids wear this uniform.

148
00:12:56.526 --> 00:12:57.527
It's nothing...

149
00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.196
I never did anything for you.

150
00:13:01.197 --> 00:13:02.907
Don't say that.

151
00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:12.083
When your dad died out of the blue,
I should have died too...

152
00:13:13.042 --> 00:13:14.251
Not that again.

153
00:13:15.378 --> 00:13:18.130
It's been over 10 years,
that's enough.

154
00:13:18.673 --> 00:13:22.385
Yeah, I'm so glad to be alive.

155
00:13:23.177 --> 00:13:25.722
I got to see you
all grown up like this.

156
00:13:29.684 --> 00:13:31.560
I'm gonna go,
get to bed early.

157
00:13:31.561 --> 00:13:33.229
You're not staying
for the night?

158
00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:36.774
I came to pick up some books.

159
00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:43.448
Yeah, dorms must be comfier.

160
00:13:46.784 --> 00:13:47.535
I'm off.

161
00:13:54.751 --> 00:13:56.002
Ji-woo.

162
00:13:57.587 --> 00:13:58.963
Is everything okay?

163
00:14:00.297 --> 00:14:01.007
Yeah.

164
00:14:09.098 --> 00:14:10.392
Go to bed early.

165
00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.609
Who's there?

166
00:15:45.612 --> 00:15:46.738
Come on out.

167
00:15:58.625 --> 00:16:00.042
What are you doing there?

168
00:16:06.257 --> 00:16:09.051
Please let me stay
until the rain stops.

169
00:16:09.844 --> 00:16:11.095
Get back to the dorm.

170
00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:14.681
I can't.

171
00:16:14.682 --> 00:16:15.432
What?

172
00:16:21.814 --> 00:16:23.983
I can't go because of you!

173
00:16:29.697 --> 00:16:31.908
My parents went on a trip.

174
00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:35.202
They left without
leaving me a key...

175
00:16:40.166 --> 00:16:44.169
Honestly, had you let me go,
I wouldn't need to be here...

176
00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.880
If you're gonna yap,
get the hell out!

177
00:17:42.604 --> 00:17:45.521
- What time...
- Wake the hell up!

178
00:17:45.522 --> 00:17:47.024
Get out, this isn't your home!

179
00:17:48.025 --> 00:17:49.736
Get out, go away!

180
00:17:50.319 --> 00:17:52.989
He could've let me
sleep a bit more...

181
00:17:57.576 --> 00:17:58.911
Stupid commie...

182
00:18:11.716 --> 00:18:13.675
Okay, let's go over the answers.

183
00:18:13.676 --> 00:18:15.093
From the front.

184
00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:16.803
#1 is 60.

185
00:18:16.804 --> 00:18:19.555
- #2 is 2.5x.
- 2.5x, okay.

186
00:18:19.556 --> 00:18:20.641
#3 is 2.

187
00:18:20.642 --> 00:18:22.977
No, no, no!
It's -2, get it together.

188
00:18:24.937 --> 00:18:26.438
Who's next?

189
00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:29.816
Ji-woo, will you snap out of it?

190
00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:31.068
What? Oh...

191
00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.782
- 6.
- What?

192
00:18:37.074 --> 00:18:38.450
The answer is 6.

193
00:18:41.162 --> 00:18:44.622
You actually did the work,
that was a tough question.

194
00:18:44.623 --> 00:18:46.207
Okay, next.

195
00:18:46.208 --> 00:18:48.669
5 is -tan theta.

196
00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:49.671
Okay!

197
00:18:50.379 --> 00:18:52.674
Good work, who got them all?

198
00:18:55.885 --> 00:18:56.427
Eh?

199
00:18:57.970 --> 00:18:58.721
Him!

200
00:19:00.097 --> 00:19:01.015
Shush!

201
00:19:16.781 --> 00:19:18.157
You did this, right?

202
00:19:26.582 --> 00:19:27.666
Thank you.

203
00:19:30.336 --> 00:19:33.630
How did you solve these?

204
00:19:38.761 --> 00:19:39.345
Out.

205
00:19:40.054 --> 00:19:40.805
Out!

206
00:19:49.271 --> 00:19:51.190
I just can't...

207
00:20:09.751 --> 00:20:10.417
Hey!

208
00:20:11.543 --> 00:20:14.088
What the heck is wrong
with our math teacher?

209
00:20:14.588 --> 00:20:17.340
Why is he giving us
impossible problems?

210
00:20:17.341 --> 00:20:19.050
This isn't some genius school.

211
00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:21.511
Even my elite private tutor
got 7 problems wrong.

212
00:20:21.512 --> 00:20:23.430
He graduated from
Seoul Univ. With honors.

213
00:20:24.431 --> 00:20:28.352
Heard about everyone going on
math bootcamps on weekends?

214
00:20:29.979 --> 00:20:31.773
Hello, I'm from the other...

215
00:20:32.564 --> 00:20:34.776
I wanted to ask you
about problem #17 here...

216
00:20:40.364 --> 00:20:41.866
What the hell
is that punk doing?

217
00:20:44.994 --> 00:20:45.702
Hey!

218
00:20:46.913 --> 00:20:48.080
What are you doing?

219
00:20:48.831 --> 00:20:49.665
Go away!

220
00:21:02.845 --> 00:21:04.763
Is the problem #18...

221
00:21:08.017 --> 00:21:08.725
Dammit.

222
00:21:10.727 --> 00:21:12.562
Yeah, think it over.

223
00:21:12.563 --> 00:21:14.190
- Here he comes.
- Go on.

224
00:21:17.401 --> 00:21:18.485
Jeez.

225
00:21:20.737 --> 00:21:21.989
What did he say?

226
00:21:22.489 --> 00:21:24.033
He'll give it a thought.

227
00:21:24.533 --> 00:21:26.035
Don't you have one too?

228
00:21:26.743 --> 00:21:28.287
Yes, Han Ji-woo.

229
00:21:29.455 --> 00:21:32.916
It's brutal, a single mother
and living in poverty...

230
00:21:32.917 --> 00:21:36.544
Transferring isn't something
he can decide on his own.

231
00:21:36.545 --> 00:21:39.756
What can he do?
His guardian doesn't care.

232
00:21:40.967 --> 00:21:43.801
Welfare system is just too cruel.

233
00:21:43.802 --> 00:21:45.011
It's not just cruel.

234
00:21:45.012 --> 00:21:49.307
Some parents love that
they fill up the lowest tier.

235
00:21:49.308 --> 00:21:51.684
But others don't want them
ruining the mood here.

236
00:21:51.685 --> 00:21:53.979
They're a chore too.

237
00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:56.190
We need to apply
scholarship for them,

238
00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:59.902
can't even joke with them,
in fear of hurting feelings.

239
00:22:00.402 --> 00:22:03.990
Yeah, his eyes fill up with sorrow
at the mention of transfer.

240
00:22:04.615 --> 00:22:07.409
I could never tell
if he's angry or hurt.

241
00:22:08.285 --> 00:22:10.286
I get more nervous.

242
00:22:10.287 --> 00:22:15.083
Coming from those families,
they got inferiority complex.

243
00:22:15.084 --> 00:22:18.087
Students from rich families
got genial personalities.

244
00:22:20.381 --> 00:22:23.675
Do you remember me?
It's about the math problem...

245
00:22:25.302 --> 00:22:28.014
No, that's too weird...

246
00:22:30.266 --> 00:22:31.976
- Hello.
- Why are you here?

247
00:22:34.686 --> 00:22:35.646
Hello.

248
00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:42.236
Teach you math?

249
00:22:42.904 --> 00:22:44.487
What the hell for?

250
00:22:44.488 --> 00:22:45.613
You know...

251
00:22:45.614 --> 00:22:47.909
Raise your grades?

252
00:22:50.077 --> 00:22:52.662
Yes, to be honest.

253
00:22:52.663 --> 00:22:58.961
Then go to a good college,
get a well-paying job?

254
00:22:59.545 --> 00:23:02.881
Yeah, in the long run.

255
00:23:04.258 --> 00:23:05.259
Transfer.

256
00:23:05.884 --> 00:23:10.055
Transfer and get your grades up.

257
00:23:10.056 --> 00:23:16.562
Wouldn't you rather be
a frog in a pond?

258
00:23:17.188 --> 00:23:19.522
But how did you...

259
00:23:19.523 --> 00:23:23.819
Aren't everyone here experts
at college entrance exam?

260
00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:26.196
Transfer out of here.

261
00:23:26.197 --> 00:23:27.073
Never!

262
00:23:30.117 --> 00:23:32.368
My mom will be disappointed.

263
00:23:32.369 --> 00:23:34.537
She was so happy
that I got into this school.

264
00:23:34.538 --> 00:23:35.539
And dad?

265
00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:38.167
He won't be disappointed?

266
00:23:41.212 --> 00:23:42.421
He passed away.

267
00:23:49.761 --> 00:23:51.305
Didn't he go on a trip?

268
00:23:52.056 --> 00:23:56.477
I'm sorry, I was just
making things up.

269
00:24:00.522 --> 00:24:02.358
How did he die?

270
00:24:04.110 --> 00:24:05.860
Do I have to answer that?

271
00:24:05.861 --> 00:24:09.531
Of course not,
isn't this a free country?

272
00:24:14.703 --> 00:24:16.788
He was hit by a drunk driver.

273
00:24:18.874 --> 00:24:22.378
He was crossing the street,
and died instantly.

274
00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:24.713
When I was 6.

275
00:24:26.423 --> 00:24:29.009
I hardly remember it,
happy now?

276
00:24:29.010 --> 00:24:32.553
Your dad dying isn't
some badge of honor.

277
00:24:32.554 --> 00:24:33.429
What did you say?

278
00:24:33.430 --> 00:24:36.058
You think you're the most
tragic person alive?

279
00:24:37.809 --> 00:24:41.313
Self-pity is a terrible disease.

280
00:24:41.938 --> 00:24:46.152
Even if you feel happy,
you'll be fixated on tragedy.

281
00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:55.536
I'm just angry.

282
00:24:59.831 --> 00:25:01.792
Everyone took extra classes,

283
00:25:03.627 --> 00:25:05.129
but I never could...

284
00:25:07.005 --> 00:25:10.175
I hung in there
by saying it's okay.

285
00:25:10.176 --> 00:25:15.222
But no matter what I did,
it was pointless.

286
00:25:20.644 --> 00:25:21.520
Forget it.

287
00:25:23.564 --> 00:25:25.191
Take this with you.

288
00:25:29.986 --> 00:25:30.904
Look here.

289
00:25:34.408 --> 00:25:36.618
Get me strawberry milk
instead tomorrow.

290
00:25:42.208 --> 00:25:44.917
Science Building B103

291
00:25:44.918 --> 00:25:46.920
Daesung Recycling

292
00:25:50.216 --> 00:25:54.135
Come work here
instead of working night shifts.

293
00:25:54.136 --> 00:25:56.596
This is just a junkyard.

294
00:25:56.597 --> 00:25:59.390
Don't hurt my feelings.

295
00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:02.811
All my employees got
permanent positions.

296
00:26:03.312 --> 00:26:07.148
If you got money to hire me,
give them raises instead.

297
00:26:07.149 --> 00:26:11.152
I'm still Southwestern Seoul's
North Korean defector support lead.

298
00:26:11.153 --> 00:26:12.945
I can at least take care of you.

299
00:26:12.946 --> 00:26:14.281
No need.

300
00:26:15.657 --> 00:26:18.369
That stubbornness of yours...

301
00:26:19.870 --> 00:26:21.205
Is it ready?

302
00:26:23.707 --> 00:26:28.503
I like to think that
my fellow North Korean defectors

303
00:26:28.504 --> 00:26:32.590
Writer Park Pil-ju, Kim Il-sung Univ. Graduate
are agents of reunification

304
00:26:32.591 --> 00:26:34.550
that bridge both nations.

305
00:26:34.551 --> 00:26:37.094
Yes, that's what I think too.

306
00:26:37.095 --> 00:26:41.224
The studio is filling up
with positive vibe.

307
00:26:41.225 --> 00:26:43.435
Which subjects are taught there?

308
00:26:44.145 --> 00:26:47.897
Literature, English, math,
physics, chemistry,

309
00:26:47.898 --> 00:26:49.775
and most important of all...

310
00:26:55.697 --> 00:26:58.074
I said I'd buy you new stuff...

311
00:26:59.701 --> 00:27:01.119
Let's take a look.

312
00:27:02.204 --> 00:27:03.872
They all look fine.

313
00:27:04.373 --> 00:27:05.582
Hold them for a sec.

314
00:27:08.169 --> 00:27:10.879
Hey, don't be like that,
we're better than this.

315
00:27:12.589 --> 00:27:16.009
I didn't do anything
to contribute to this country,

316
00:27:17.386 --> 00:27:19.263
I can never take things for free.

317
00:27:21.598 --> 00:27:22.433
Take it.

318
00:27:23.892 --> 00:27:24.810
Take it!

319
00:27:29.606 --> 00:27:34.944
Oh yeah, your ledger's all wrong.

320
00:27:34.945 --> 00:27:36.362
What? Again?

321
00:27:36.363 --> 00:27:38.532
You added 43 cents more.

322
00:28:13.567 --> 00:28:15.151
B103...

323
00:28:37.341 --> 00:28:38.925
Did you bring them?

324
00:28:45.474 --> 00:28:46.642
Come in.

325
00:28:49.102 --> 00:28:51.145
I solved from here to here...

326
00:28:51.146 --> 00:28:52.356
Promise me.

327
00:28:55.233 --> 00:28:56.527
Rule 1.

328
00:28:57.278 --> 00:29:01.489
Do not ever tell anyone
what goes on here.

329
00:29:01.490 --> 00:29:03.616
Yes, of course.

330
00:29:03.617 --> 00:29:05.035
Rule 2.

331
00:29:05.577 --> 00:29:07.954
No questions other than math.

332
00:29:09.122 --> 00:29:10.415
Rule 3.

333
00:29:10.416 --> 00:29:12.834
I will teach you math,

334
00:29:13.544 --> 00:29:15.754
but I'm not interested in
tests or your grades.

335
00:29:19.550 --> 00:29:20.216
Okay.

336
00:29:30.477 --> 00:29:31.645
Look at this.

337
00:29:34.398 --> 00:29:38.151
Here's a triangle
with points A, B, C.

338
00:29:39.486 --> 00:29:44.616
With A at 90 degrees,
it's an isosceles right triangle.

339
00:29:45.200 --> 00:29:49.036
Height is 6
and base is 10.

340
00:29:49.037 --> 00:29:50.664
Define the area.

341
00:29:54.793 --> 00:29:57.086
This is an elementary problem.

342
00:29:57.087 --> 00:29:58.714
So you don't know.

343
00:29:59.756 --> 00:30:00.840
It's 30.

344
00:30:00.841 --> 00:30:03.092
You really are dense.

345
00:30:03.093 --> 00:30:04.552
Which elementary school
did you attend?

346
00:30:04.553 --> 00:30:05.387
What?

347
00:30:07.764 --> 00:30:09.140
I'm right, it's 30.

348
00:30:16.064 --> 00:30:19.692
Base times height,
divided by 2.

349
00:30:19.693 --> 00:30:20.902
It's 30...

350
00:30:37.503 --> 00:30:40.255
Look carefully.

351
00:30:48.597 --> 00:30:53.935
The height is the radius,
so it should be 5, not 6.

352
00:30:55.937 --> 00:30:58.231
You're not full-on stupid.

353
00:30:59.983 --> 00:31:03.027
Come on, you gave me
an incorrect question.

354
00:31:03.028 --> 00:31:05.822
In South Korea,
we call it question error.

355
00:31:06.573 --> 00:31:08.365
They give you a pass
if it popped up on a test.

356
00:31:08.366 --> 00:31:13.455
Rule 3, I'm not interested in
tests or your grades.

357
00:31:14.122 --> 00:31:18.083
So does this triangle
exist or not?

358
00:31:18.084 --> 00:31:19.752
It can't exist.

359
00:31:19.753 --> 00:31:24.925
So how does an idiot
insists that the area is 30?

360
00:31:25.759 --> 00:31:28.511
You insisted it 3 times.

361
00:31:28.512 --> 00:31:31.013
I never insisted 3 times.

362
00:31:31.014 --> 00:31:31.847
It's 30.

363
00:31:31.848 --> 00:31:32.891
I'm right, it's 30.

364
00:31:33.391 --> 00:31:34.309
It's 30...

365
00:31:37.646 --> 00:31:42.191
Who knew you'd intentionally
give me an incorrect question?

366
00:31:42.192 --> 00:31:48.198
It's because you were so blind
to solving problems.

367
00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:51.534
Finding the answer is important,

368
00:31:51.535 --> 00:31:54.204
but knowing what the problem is
even more important.

369
00:31:55.622 --> 00:32:00.126
You can't get the right answer
from an incorrect problem.

370
00:32:01.252 --> 00:32:02.212
Ergo!

371
00:32:05.591 --> 00:32:10.679
It's all about the process
of finding the solution,

372
00:32:11.805 --> 00:32:14.641
that's math, got that?

373
00:32:15.684 --> 00:32:16.309
Yes.

374
00:32:17.393 --> 00:32:18.562
Epsilon.

375
00:32:19.437 --> 00:32:20.606
Epsilon?

376
00:32:21.356 --> 00:32:23.149
What's that?

377
00:32:37.539 --> 00:32:39.415
Small and insignificant,

378
00:32:40.542 --> 00:32:42.210
infinitely small...

379
00:32:46.923 --> 00:32:47.924
Small?

380
00:32:52.053 --> 00:32:54.097
Petty and trivial being.

381
00:32:57.726 --> 00:32:58.727
Trivial...

382
00:33:16.119 --> 00:33:17.871
Why are you following me?

383
00:33:21.082 --> 00:33:23.209
I have to sleep,
it's getting late.

384
00:33:24.753 --> 00:33:26.337
No more buses.

385
00:33:33.136 --> 00:33:35.513
Don't you dare touch
my lesson fee.

386
00:33:37.390 --> 00:33:39.434
I don't even care...

387
00:33:44.022 --> 00:33:45.356
Out of the way.

388
00:33:49.319 --> 00:33:51.905
Did you defect
for strawberry milk?

389
00:33:56.785 --> 00:33:58.119
Is this a radio?

390
00:34:05.126 --> 00:34:05.919
Wow.

391
00:34:06.461 --> 00:34:08.922
This is so cool!

392
00:34:10.006 --> 00:34:11.674
What music is that?

393
00:34:11.675 --> 00:34:14.802
Johann Sebastian Bach.

394
00:34:14.803 --> 00:34:15.970
Bach?

395
00:34:15.971 --> 00:34:20.307
Him, the father of
classical music.

396
00:34:20.308 --> 00:34:23.185
You don't know his music,
how could you call him that?

397
00:34:23.186 --> 00:34:25.856
I know the mother
of music too, it's Handel.

398
00:34:26.522 --> 00:34:27.691
Uncle?

399
00:34:28.775 --> 00:34:30.525
Schubert?

400
00:34:30.526 --> 00:34:31.612
Beethoven.

401
00:34:32.362 --> 00:34:33.655
Come on...

402
00:34:36.241 --> 00:34:38.326
The sound quality is...

403
00:34:47.335 --> 00:34:49.337
Isn't this better?

404
00:34:50.338 --> 00:34:52.548
It'd be better if it's louder.

405
00:35:03.935 --> 00:35:05.270
Much better?

406
00:35:25.581 --> 00:35:26.582
Aren't you going to sleep?

407
00:35:27.125 --> 00:35:28.125
What?

408
00:35:28.126 --> 00:35:32.338
There's a blanket there,
pass out here.

409
00:35:48.354 --> 00:35:50.023
Do you like Bach?

410
00:35:52.608 --> 00:35:55.570
He is the beginning
and end of music.

411
00:35:59.615 --> 00:36:03.203
I can kinda see that,
but the end too?

412
00:36:06.289 --> 00:36:08.875
Even if humanity
cease to exist,

413
00:36:10.251 --> 00:36:14.464
all music can be recreated
with Bach's sheet music.

414
00:36:24.725 --> 00:36:29.687
Why did you defect
from North Korea?

415
00:36:32.565 --> 00:36:34.067
Did you come alone?

416
00:36:35.610 --> 00:36:36.318
Your family...

417
00:36:36.319 --> 00:36:39.197
No questions other than math.

418
00:36:44.369 --> 00:36:46.621
You talked plenty about Bach...

419
00:36:52.753 --> 00:36:54.045
Mr. Park! Wake up!

420
00:36:54.629 --> 00:36:56.047
Shift rotation time.

421
00:36:57.423 --> 00:36:58.299
Huh?

422
00:37:05.974 --> 00:37:07.516
It's not like you.

423
00:37:07.517 --> 00:37:09.352
You actually slept well?

424
00:37:14.274 --> 00:37:15.817
Pythagoras.

425
00:37:16.317 --> 00:37:17.819
Award.

426
00:37:19.279 --> 00:37:23.532
It's Donghun Academy's
greatest math competition.

427
00:37:23.533 --> 00:37:26.160
It's not like tests
you take day in and out.

428
00:37:26.161 --> 00:37:28.913
You take it only once
at the end of grade 10.

429
00:37:28.914 --> 00:37:32.876
Renowned outside teachers
will create and mark them.

430
00:37:33.709 --> 00:37:34.960
Eui-joon.

431
00:37:34.961 --> 00:37:37.254
Will it be awarded
to 3 students again?

432
00:37:37.255 --> 00:37:40.341
Of course, gold, silver and bronze.

433
00:37:40.842 --> 00:37:41.675
Too harsh.

434
00:37:41.676 --> 00:37:45.930
You won gold at
International Mathematical Olympiad?

435
00:37:45.931 --> 00:37:49.099
That's useless for college,
only school awards can be listed.

436
00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:50.977
You won a Nobel Prize?

437
00:37:51.561 --> 00:37:53.478
It won't help you get into college.

438
00:37:53.479 --> 00:37:57.358
But what about Pythagoras Award?

439
00:37:58.109 --> 00:38:00.195
It's usable,
it'll be on your record!

440
00:38:00.987 --> 00:38:02.737
That's the point.

441
00:38:02.738 --> 00:38:05.658
Aside from 3 winners,
the rest are stooges.

442
00:38:06.659 --> 00:38:08.411
Good point, Bo-ram.

443
00:38:08.912 --> 00:38:12.414
So those who know they can't win
tend to just give it up.

444
00:38:12.415 --> 00:38:13.749
Academic record

445
00:38:14.792 --> 00:38:19.339
For this reason, this competition
will be turned into the final exam.

446
00:38:23.343 --> 00:38:24.844
Quiet down.

447
00:38:24.845 --> 00:38:25.803
Easy.

448
00:38:26.596 --> 00:38:28.722
You got 2 months.

449
00:38:28.723 --> 00:38:31.308
As your homeroom
and math teacher,

450
00:38:31.309 --> 00:38:35.981
I earnestly hope
my student wins the gold.

451
00:38:39.943 --> 00:38:41.236
90 cents, please.

452
00:38:52.330 --> 00:38:54.040
You got an addiction?

453
00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:55.791
Yup.

454
00:39:01.297 --> 00:39:02.797
So it was an addiction.

455
00:39:02.798 --> 00:39:06.218
What is S sub 10 at the least?

456
00:39:06.219 --> 00:39:09.054
I'm confused,
if you could explain...

457
00:39:09.055 --> 00:39:12.600
What's there to explain?
Just add it all up.

458
00:39:13.601 --> 00:39:14.726
I know that, but...

459
00:39:14.727 --> 00:39:17.146
Forget it, just solve it.

460
00:39:17.147 --> 00:39:20.400
So add them all up manually
like a chump?

461
00:39:21.692 --> 00:39:22.776
Why not?

462
00:39:22.777 --> 00:39:23.403
What?

463
00:39:24.070 --> 00:39:26.907
Everything manually? Really?

464
00:39:28.324 --> 00:39:29.450
Of course.

465
00:39:44.132 --> 00:39:45.550
I think I solved it.

466
00:39:47.510 --> 00:39:48.761
Come over here.

467
00:39:52.557 --> 00:39:53.975
Look at this.

468
00:39:55.268 --> 00:39:57.186
What was he solving for?

469
00:39:57.187 --> 00:39:59.564
1.414...

470
00:40:00.356 --> 00:40:01.565
Square root of 2?

471
00:40:01.566 --> 00:40:02.358
Right.

472
00:40:03.276 --> 00:40:08.031
He calculated 38 decimals
of square root of 2 all by hand.

473
00:40:08.656 --> 00:40:12.660
He could've just put
square root of 2...

474
00:40:13.828 --> 00:40:14.996
What a perv.

475
00:40:15.913 --> 00:40:22.377
This perv is none other than
Georg Friedrich Bernhard Riemann.

476
00:40:22.378 --> 00:40:26.256
Riemann? As in
Riemann Hypothesis?

477
00:40:26.257 --> 00:40:29.468
You sure know a lot of
useless stuff for a dumb kid.

478
00:40:29.469 --> 00:40:32.512
It's a hypothesis about prime numbers...

479
00:40:32.513 --> 00:40:34.390
It hasn't been proven yet, right?

480
00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:36.267
Well...

481
00:40:36.892 --> 00:40:37.893
It has?

482
00:40:38.686 --> 00:40:40.395
The real question is,

483
00:40:40.396 --> 00:40:44.274
why did this world
renowned mathematician

484
00:40:44.275 --> 00:40:50.197
worked on a useless calculation,
such as square root of 2?

485
00:40:50.198 --> 00:40:51.491
Indeed!

486
00:40:53.951 --> 00:40:55.703
To become intimate.

487
00:40:56.454 --> 00:40:57.997
With square root of 2?

488
00:40:57.998 --> 00:41:03.377
You can't do that
by memorizing a formula.

489
00:41:03.378 --> 00:41:06.881
You have to get down
and befriend it

490
00:41:07.798 --> 00:41:10.426
to understand, then love it.

491
00:41:11.052 --> 00:41:13.095
But how could you
calculate it all every time?

492
00:41:13.096 --> 00:41:15.140
It's not about the calculation.

493
00:41:16.141 --> 00:41:17.017
Think.

494
00:41:18.768 --> 00:41:23.564
Make an effort and slowly,
think with utmost effort.

495
00:41:27.860 --> 00:41:30.155
Do you feel more intimate?

496
00:41:30.655 --> 00:41:32.907
Well... a bit...

497
00:41:36.619 --> 00:41:38.078
So what's the answer?

498
00:41:38.079 --> 00:41:39.955
Why are you asking me that?

499
00:41:40.498 --> 00:41:42.249
You came up with that answer.

500
00:41:42.250 --> 00:41:44.626
You have to confirm it,
who else?

501
00:41:44.627 --> 00:41:45.461
What?

502
00:41:46.129 --> 00:41:50.840
Solving a problem without a solution,
checking to see if it's right,

503
00:41:50.841 --> 00:41:54.053
and proving it is the job
of a mathematician.

504
00:41:54.054 --> 00:41:59.266
Wait, I'm not a mathematician,
I'm a math reject.

505
00:41:59.267 --> 00:42:01.017
It took me 3 hours
to solve this,

506
00:42:01.018 --> 00:42:02.352
if I solve test problems like this...

507
00:42:02.353 --> 00:42:03.646
Rule 3.

508
00:42:04.564 --> 00:42:05.398
Tell me.

509
00:42:06.191 --> 00:42:09.068
Not interested in tests
or grades.

510
00:42:09.069 --> 00:42:09.944
Very good.

511
00:42:11.362 --> 00:42:12.737
Homework.

512
00:42:12.738 --> 00:42:14.490
Check and see if it's right.

513
00:42:18.119 --> 00:42:20.205
Calculus
Probability and Statistics

514
00:43:35.112 --> 00:43:36.197
Yo, dumb-ass.

515
00:43:40.618 --> 00:43:44.539
You turned into a homeless
only a month after the boot.

516
00:43:45.331 --> 00:43:48.584
Mister, you can't sleep here.

517
00:43:49.169 --> 00:43:50.336
You got a visitation.

518
00:43:54.382 --> 00:43:55.965
Where will you go?

519
00:43:55.966 --> 00:43:57.468
A regular high school
near my home.

520
00:43:59.053 --> 00:44:01.597
Your family don't feel bad about it?

521
00:44:05.393 --> 00:44:08.354
My grandma doesn't know
about college admission.

522
00:44:09.814 --> 00:44:12.692
I shouldn't have come here.

523
00:44:14.360 --> 00:44:16.237
I know it's not my place,

524
00:44:17.029 --> 00:44:20.574
but you should think it over
before it's too late.

525
00:44:20.575 --> 00:44:24.704
Please follow rules
when picking up your child...

526
00:44:33.421 --> 00:44:35.130
Will you transfer too?

527
00:44:36.341 --> 00:44:37.633
Can you piss off?

528
00:44:38.301 --> 00:44:41.804
Helping welfare recipients
transfer out is all the rage.

529
00:44:43.514 --> 00:44:44.515
Having fun?

530
00:44:46.309 --> 00:44:48.060
Messing with welfare recipients?

531
00:44:50.020 --> 00:44:51.771
I'm in the same boat too.

532
00:44:51.772 --> 00:44:53.858
Same boat? You serious?

533
00:44:54.359 --> 00:44:59.154
You and I are nothing alike,
you're on a yacht.

534
00:45:01.741 --> 00:45:02.366
But...

535
00:45:02.367 --> 00:45:03.368
Bo-ram!

536
00:45:09.749 --> 00:45:10.500
Hey...

537
00:45:14.629 --> 00:45:15.963
Who was he?

538
00:45:19.216 --> 00:45:20.509
A welfare recipient.

539
00:45:20.510 --> 00:45:23.471
After all I did to enroll you,
you hang out with him?

540
00:45:25.515 --> 00:45:28.393
What's wrong with
2 welfare recipients hanging out?

541
00:45:28.893 --> 00:45:32.355
Nope, you're a welfare recipient
without financial aid.

542
00:45:33.398 --> 00:45:36.232
Parents divorcing and
being a douche is a reward,

543
00:45:36.233 --> 00:45:38.693
but studying hard
in a low-income family is a stigma?

544
00:45:38.694 --> 00:45:40.236
Who said it was a stigma?

545
00:45:40.237 --> 00:45:42.238
You don't want me
to be friends with him.

546
00:45:42.239 --> 00:45:45.576
He's not socially assisted,
he's discriminated.

547
00:45:47.662 --> 00:45:50.331
Anyway, I changed
your math tutor as of today.

548
00:45:51.582 --> 00:45:52.417
Again?

549
00:45:53.334 --> 00:45:57.128
Math is crucial to college admission,
other subjects are useless.

550
00:45:57.129 --> 00:45:58.755
It was hard getting you in.

551
00:45:58.756 --> 00:46:00.300
Your homeroom teacher
made it happen.

552
00:46:01.509 --> 00:46:02.968
Isn't that illegal?

553
00:46:04.053 --> 00:46:06.514
He's looking out for you,
be thankful.

554
00:46:07.473 --> 00:46:09.684
I heard the Pythagoras
will replace the finals.

555
00:46:14.314 --> 00:46:18.443
Everything leaks in real time
at this damn school.

556
00:46:19.360 --> 00:46:20.986
The tutor is supposedly amazing.

557
00:46:22.029 --> 00:46:24.490
It's an elite class with
top of the top students.

558
00:46:33.290 --> 00:46:34.417
That's enough.

559
00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:37.294
I told you to stop piano
for your own sake!

560
00:46:43.968 --> 00:46:46.803
Euler Math Research Lab
Eh? A research lab?

561
00:46:46.804 --> 00:46:50.933
Like I said, an elite class,
it's very expensive.

562
00:47:05.573 --> 00:47:06.991
What are you doing?

563
00:47:08.117 --> 00:47:11.537
I think I understand
why you do this.

564
00:47:13.456 --> 00:47:15.458
I feel at ease.

565
00:47:16.792 --> 00:47:19.086
Stop fooling around
and hit the books.

566
00:47:27.970 --> 00:47:30.264
A friend of mine transferred out,

567
00:47:32.099 --> 00:47:33.851
he was on welfare too.

568
00:47:37.813 --> 00:47:44.486
My teacher isn't completely wrong
when he told me to transfer.

569
00:47:44.487 --> 00:47:46.531
But he's not right either.

570
00:47:48.574 --> 00:47:51.160
Don't believe anything
that aren't proven.

571
00:47:52.286 --> 00:47:54.789
That's what mathematicians do.

572
00:48:00.210 --> 00:48:01.336
Look here.

573
00:48:02.129 --> 00:48:06.926
What do you need the most
to be good at math?

574
00:48:07.468 --> 00:48:09.052
Being smart, probably.

575
00:48:09.053 --> 00:48:11.514
Smart people give up first.

576
00:48:12.056 --> 00:48:15.767
I hope you don't mean 'effort'.

577
00:48:15.768 --> 00:48:19.522
Those who rely on effort
give up next.

578
00:48:20.481 --> 00:48:21.941
Then what is it?

579
00:48:23.443 --> 00:48:24.359
Courage.

580
00:48:27.738 --> 00:48:30.699
"Come on! I can do it!"
stuff like that?

581
00:48:30.700 --> 00:48:32.493
That's bravado.

582
00:48:33.453 --> 00:48:37.289
Rather than get angry or give up
when you can't solve a problem,

583
00:48:37.873 --> 00:48:41.125
you say to yourself,

584
00:48:41.126 --> 00:48:44.839
"This is really tough,
I'll try again tomorrow."

585
00:48:46.466 --> 00:48:48.383
That's mathematical courage.

586
00:48:49.176 --> 00:48:53.430
Those with composed
and firm personalities

587
00:48:54.849 --> 00:48:57.392
prevail in the end.

588
00:48:59.061 --> 00:49:01.271
That's a far cry for me.

589
00:49:05.610 --> 00:49:06.861
I'm talking about you.

590
00:49:09.071 --> 00:49:10.072
Take a look.

591
00:49:17.246 --> 00:49:19.248
There are more wrongs.

592
00:49:19.790 --> 00:49:23.043
There are indeed,
but the process is right.

593
00:49:24.128 --> 00:49:25.671
Do not transfer.

594
00:49:26.255 --> 00:49:30.801
You got here this far
without giving up.

595
00:49:33.095 --> 00:49:34.346
That's all you needed to do.

596
00:49:35.347 --> 00:49:36.348
So...

597
00:49:37.517 --> 00:49:38.643
prove it,

598
00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:41.979
whether transfer is right or not.

599
00:49:42.688 --> 00:49:43.564
Got it?

600
00:49:46.734 --> 00:49:48.110
Head on in.

601
00:49:53.365 --> 00:49:54.909
Aren't you sad?

602
00:49:55.993 --> 00:49:57.452
We lived together for a month.

603
00:49:58.370 --> 00:49:59.664
Buzz off.

604
00:50:13.719 --> 00:50:16.805
Hearts do not linger at home,

605
00:50:16.806 --> 00:50:21.018
but drifts to the distant port
like clouds.

606
00:50:32.780 --> 00:50:34.949
Yo Dumbass,
sorry about last time!

607
00:50:58.138 --> 00:51:00.556
So reduce -6 to
a common denominator,

608
00:51:00.557 --> 00:51:03.059
and turn it into -12/2,

609
00:51:03.060 --> 00:51:04.687
then 11/2 plus...

610
00:51:11.986 --> 00:51:13.362
Where did you come from?

611
00:51:13.988 --> 00:51:14.822
Hey!

612
00:51:17.491 --> 00:51:20.661
- Why are you...
- Out, could you leave?

613
00:51:22.913 --> 00:51:24.038
The commie officer?

614
00:51:24.039 --> 00:51:24.831
No way!

615
00:51:24.832 --> 00:51:25.915
Go! Right now!

616
00:51:25.916 --> 00:51:26.876
Wait a minute.

617
00:51:28.585 --> 00:51:30.378
Good evening.

618
00:51:30.379 --> 00:51:32.631
I'm so sorry for startling you.

619
00:51:32.632 --> 00:51:34.340
A skull fell out of nowhere.

620
00:51:34.341 --> 00:51:35.425
Come on!

621
00:51:36.844 --> 00:51:39.262
I'm his classmate,

622
00:51:39.263 --> 00:51:41.931
my name is Bo-ram,
Park Bo-ram.

623
00:51:41.932 --> 00:51:43.017
Could you leave?

624
00:51:50.065 --> 00:51:51.608
I heard so much about you.

625
00:51:52.276 --> 00:51:54.568
No, I never said a word to her!

626
00:51:54.569 --> 00:51:56.905
I didn't say anything to you,
I really didn't!

627
00:51:56.906 --> 00:52:00.325
Even though he's dumb,
you're looking out for him,

628
00:52:01.786 --> 00:52:03.787
I don't know how to thank you.

629
00:52:03.788 --> 00:52:07.165
What is wrong with you?
I'm sorry about everything!

630
00:52:07.166 --> 00:52:07.916
Please...

631
00:52:07.917 --> 00:52:08.876
That's hot...

632
00:52:09.459 --> 00:52:10.878
Please take care of him.

633
00:52:11.378 --> 00:52:12.628
Stop saying that!

634
00:52:12.629 --> 00:52:13.756
Don't listen to her!

635
00:52:14.548 --> 00:52:15.507
Actually...

636
00:52:18.593 --> 00:52:19.510
I like him.

637
00:52:19.511 --> 00:52:20.304
What?!

638
00:52:20.888 --> 00:52:22.848
He's so genuine
and loyal too.

639
00:52:23.557 --> 00:52:24.391
Right?

640
00:52:26.643 --> 00:52:29.354
You must really like
strawberry milk.

641
00:52:30.564 --> 00:52:32.316
Should I get some next time?

642
00:52:33.901 --> 00:52:35.234
Could I come by sometimes?

643
00:52:35.235 --> 00:52:37.570
No way, you know you can't.

644
00:52:37.571 --> 00:52:38.612
Of course.

645
00:52:38.613 --> 00:52:40.239
If you keep your secret.

646
00:52:40.240 --> 00:52:40.990
Let's go.

647
00:52:40.991 --> 00:52:43.493
Eh? That was easy.

648
00:52:45.579 --> 00:52:47.663
Hey, you really can't
tell anyone about this.

649
00:52:47.664 --> 00:52:49.333
- I'm not like you!
- Jesus!

650
00:52:51.543 --> 00:52:54.462
No way, I didn't say anything!
I'm serious.

651
00:52:54.463 --> 00:52:59.093
By the way,
why am I a commie officer?

652
00:53:00.052 --> 00:53:01.804
Because...

653
00:53:02.596 --> 00:53:04.638
you came from North Korea?

654
00:53:04.639 --> 00:53:06.224
But I never served
in the military.

655
00:53:06.225 --> 00:53:10.020
What? Seriously?
You got exempted?

656
00:53:11.021 --> 00:53:14.315
Cool, you're a golden parachute.

657
00:53:14.316 --> 00:53:16.235
Eh? What's going on?

658
00:53:17.361 --> 00:53:18.362
What are they doing?

659
00:53:20.030 --> 00:53:22.866
Ji-woo barely finished
his punishment...

660
00:53:22.867 --> 00:53:25.494
They've got some nerves, no?

661
00:53:31.583 --> 00:53:32.625
Not gonna catch them?

662
00:53:32.626 --> 00:53:33.293
No need.

663
00:53:33.836 --> 00:53:38.547
What? How is that fair?
Only I got screwed?

664
00:53:38.548 --> 00:53:40.049
Only I got screwed?

665
00:53:40.050 --> 00:53:41.801
- Stop mimicking me.
- Stop mimicking me!

666
00:53:41.802 --> 00:53:42.927
- Stop that.
- Stop that!

667
00:53:42.928 --> 00:53:46.848
Hey, hey, why don't you two
just get married then?

668
00:53:46.849 --> 00:53:48.808
- Marry her? Come on!
- Never, ever!

669
00:53:48.809 --> 00:53:51.185
Do you know what his
nickname is? Dumbass.

670
00:53:51.186 --> 00:53:52.020
Stop it!

671
00:53:52.021 --> 00:53:54.063
Dumbass? What's dumb-ass?

672
00:53:54.064 --> 00:53:55.315
Are you an ass?

673
00:53:59.028 --> 00:54:01.989
You don't believe that
math is simple?

674
00:54:03.073 --> 00:54:06.493
Whatever, it's so complicated...

675
00:54:08.203 --> 00:54:10.329
No one probably will believe you.

676
00:54:10.330 --> 00:54:12.041
You will.

677
00:54:14.126 --> 00:54:17.379
When you realize
how complicated life is.

678
00:54:20.049 --> 00:54:22.384
Did you know
from the beginning?

679
00:54:23.635 --> 00:54:25.553
Why did you study this?

680
00:54:25.554 --> 00:54:27.014
For the scholarship.

681
00:54:29.683 --> 00:54:31.393
Very practical.

682
00:54:32.561 --> 00:54:35.147
I wanted to be ahead
of other comrades,

683
00:54:36.731 --> 00:54:40.360
and for the sake
of my family, I had to.

684
00:54:40.986 --> 00:54:42.947
That was the start,

685
00:54:44.156 --> 00:54:46.783
but I had a different reason
for continuing.

686
00:54:47.617 --> 00:54:48.828
What's that?

687
00:54:52.456 --> 00:54:54.166
Isn't it beautiful?

688
00:54:54.749 --> 00:54:55.709
What is?

689
00:55:06.220 --> 00:55:08.179
Natural number.

690
00:55:08.180 --> 00:55:11.808
All sloping lines can be
expressed with this.

691
00:55:19.399 --> 00:55:20.484
Pi.

692
00:55:21.986 --> 00:55:22.987
Circular constant.

693
00:55:30.577 --> 00:55:32.162
Imaginary number.

694
00:55:44.216 --> 00:55:46.718
Smallest natural number 1,

695
00:55:47.302 --> 00:55:50.764
and a paradoxical number 0,
that exists to express 'nil'.

696
00:55:51.598 --> 00:55:54.643
All these numbers that are
seemingly unrelated...

697
00:55:55.185 --> 00:55:57.104
are connected this way.

698
00:56:02.401 --> 00:56:06.195
When you add 1
to e to the pi times I,

699
00:56:06.196 --> 00:56:08.865
how could it end up with a zero?

700
00:56:14.371 --> 00:56:19.668
No matter how you look at it,
it is simply breathless.

701
00:56:27.592 --> 00:56:33.182
This is the formula
that Euler came up with.

702
00:56:37.686 --> 00:56:39.438
Isn't it beautiful?

703
00:56:47.904 --> 00:56:49.031
No?

704
00:56:51.575 --> 00:56:56.538
It's pretty cool,
but not beautiful...

705
00:56:58.123 --> 00:56:59.708
All right.

706
00:57:13.097 --> 00:57:14.723
Why did you call me?

707
00:57:15.640 --> 00:57:17.309
You said you can play.

708
00:57:17.892 --> 00:57:19.268
But why?

709
00:57:19.269 --> 00:57:22.897
How is math related to piano?

710
00:57:30.197 --> 00:57:32.324
I'll show you the real deal.

711
00:57:34.534 --> 00:57:35.285
Look here.

712
00:57:35.910 --> 00:57:39.372
1 is C, 2 is D, 3 is E,

713
00:57:39.373 --> 00:57:41.041
et cetera, that's how we'll play.

714
00:57:41.708 --> 00:57:45.587
I'll play the numbers,
so play the accompaniment.

715
00:57:46.213 --> 00:57:47.589
Can you do it?

716
00:58:26.420 --> 00:58:27.962
You're playing pi.

717
00:59:55.467 --> 00:59:56.218
Whoa...

718
00:59:57.302 --> 00:59:59.263
This Pi Song is amazing!

719
01:00:06.478 --> 01:00:09.897
M²-1, is this true or false?

720
01:00:09.898 --> 01:00:12.275
True? If you select that,

721
01:00:12.276 --> 01:00:14.360
you'd pick A, B, C, right?

722
01:00:14.361 --> 01:00:16.445
Then the answer is #5, okay?

723
01:00:16.446 --> 01:00:17.070
Okay.

724
01:00:17.071 --> 01:00:18.573
- Next question...
- Sir?

725
01:00:20.116 --> 01:00:21.367
Take a quick washroom break.

726
01:00:21.368 --> 01:00:24.120
I think C is false.

727
01:00:27.957 --> 01:00:32.586
Wow, now it feels like
the lesson is going places.

728
01:00:32.587 --> 01:00:36.675
Please come on out
and prove me wrong, Mr. Han.

729
01:00:50.314 --> 01:00:55.443
M=log4,

730
01:00:55.444 --> 01:00:59.656
then n=10log4 cancels 10 and log,

731
01:01:00.407 --> 01:01:02.450
so n=4,

732
01:01:02.451 --> 01:01:06.371
which means C is false, no?

733
01:01:09.833 --> 01:01:10.791
Good, very good.

734
01:01:10.792 --> 01:01:12.711
It's not without reason, however!

735
01:01:13.253 --> 01:01:15.839
The answer to this problem
is #5 for sure, why?

736
01:01:16.923 --> 01:01:18.924
Because that's
the examiner's intent.

737
01:01:18.925 --> 01:01:23.011
The examiner did not intent
for a fiddly number as m,

738
01:01:23.012 --> 01:01:24.347
but a natural number.

739
01:01:24.348 --> 01:01:27.851
Therefore, it can only be #5, okay?

740
01:01:28.352 --> 01:01:33.398
Then shouldn't he have
defined it in the problem?

741
01:01:42.241 --> 01:01:43.616
Listen, Ji-woo.

742
01:01:43.617 --> 01:01:47.328
I'm talking about test technique.

743
01:01:47.329 --> 01:01:51.499
Rather than questioning the examiner,
work on a few more problems.

744
01:01:51.500 --> 01:01:53.542
If a problem like this
pops up on the test,

745
01:01:53.543 --> 01:01:57.463
and if you defy the intent
and pick #3,

746
01:01:57.464 --> 01:01:58.922
you'd get a fail.

747
01:01:58.923 --> 01:02:01.050
Aren't examiners wrong at times?

748
01:02:02.886 --> 01:02:05.971
Examiner? Are you saying...

749
01:02:05.972 --> 01:02:09.142
Right answer can't be found
from an incorrect question.

750
01:02:14.689 --> 01:02:16.064
Okay, Han Ji-woo.

751
01:02:16.065 --> 01:02:19.402
I'm going to put this exact problem
in the next test, so you...

752
01:02:19.403 --> 01:02:22.447
Yes, my answer will be #3.

753
01:02:24.491 --> 01:02:25.409
Out.

754
01:02:32.749 --> 01:02:34.000
Listen carefully.

755
01:02:34.626 --> 01:02:37.545
There's only one job
for Korea's examinees:

756
01:02:37.546 --> 01:02:39.547
understanding the examiner's intent.

757
01:02:39.548 --> 01:02:43.176
If he says red is green,
then it's green.

758
01:02:44.093 --> 01:02:45.512
If you question that?

759
01:02:47.347 --> 01:02:49.349
It's yours to lose.

760
01:03:02.111 --> 01:03:03.029
Sir.

761
01:03:04.656 --> 01:03:09.828
I'm going to stay,
I won't transfer.

762
01:03:19.463 --> 01:03:22.757
Daesung Recycling

763
01:03:28.930 --> 01:03:30.890
You must be in a good mood.

764
01:03:32.225 --> 01:03:34.102
I've never seen
that expression on you.

765
01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.688
Stop your nonsense.

766
01:03:44.028 --> 01:03:45.989
Well, what to do...

767
01:03:48.700 --> 01:03:52.245
I'll place this right here.

768
01:03:55.457 --> 01:03:57.417
I'm so sorry about this.

769
01:03:59.628 --> 01:04:01.713
If you cling to the norm,

770
01:04:04.799 --> 01:04:06.801
you may not see
the next move.

771
01:04:10.263 --> 01:04:12.641
Let me take back a move,
this is way too...

772
01:04:13.141 --> 01:04:15.977
Let's get to work!
Time for work!

773
01:04:18.605 --> 01:04:20.482
Wait a minute, hold on.

774
01:04:22.275 --> 01:04:23.443
A gift.

775
01:04:25.361 --> 01:04:28.155
I was gonna give you this
as a consolation to losing...

776
01:04:28.156 --> 01:04:29.907
Forget about it.

777
01:04:29.908 --> 01:04:32.993
I'm doing me a favor.

778
01:04:32.994 --> 01:04:36.623
It takes so much effort
to find you and play a game.

779
01:04:37.123 --> 01:04:40.543
You can take pics
and listen to music.

780
01:04:40.544 --> 01:04:43.630
At least have basic
necessities in life.

781
01:04:45.799 --> 01:04:46.925
Thanks.

782
01:04:51.471 --> 01:04:53.305
You bought a phone?

783
01:04:53.306 --> 01:04:55.308
How amazing is that?

784
01:04:56.225 --> 01:05:00.063
I can read all theses in the world
from the palm of my hand.

785
01:05:03.149 --> 01:05:04.526
You can see that?

786
01:05:08.655 --> 01:05:09.656
Hey.

787
01:05:12.659 --> 01:05:14.409
Can you get me into the lab?

788
01:05:14.410 --> 01:05:15.953
What? No way.

789
01:05:15.954 --> 01:05:17.538
Just once.

790
01:05:17.539 --> 01:05:21.750
Tomorrow is the day of
the Pythagoras Award...

791
01:05:21.751 --> 01:05:23.712
- Good afternoon.
- Hello.

792
01:05:24.295 --> 01:05:27.005
Did something good happen?
Why are you two grinning?

793
01:05:27.006 --> 01:05:28.299
Here.

794
01:05:28.883 --> 01:05:29.968
What's this?

795
01:05:30.719 --> 01:05:32.428
A thesis, a mathematics thesis.

796
01:05:45.567 --> 01:05:46.775
I can read it on my phone...

797
01:05:46.776 --> 01:05:48.236
Aren't you thankful?

798
01:05:51.615 --> 01:05:53.699
Since you printed it,
I can't throw it out...

799
01:05:53.700 --> 01:05:54.618
Jesus!

800
01:05:55.326 --> 01:05:59.122
Just say, "Thank you, comrade."
That's all it takes!

801
01:06:01.165 --> 01:06:02.875
Good luck with
your test tomorrow.

802
01:06:02.876 --> 01:06:04.085
Rule 3,

803
01:06:05.086 --> 01:06:08.338
you're not interested in
tests or grades, no?

804
01:06:08.339 --> 01:06:09.173
Look here.

805
01:06:09.841 --> 01:06:12.718
I can be disinterested
in your tests,

806
01:06:12.719 --> 01:06:15.929
but you shouldn't be
disinterested in yours.

807
01:06:15.930 --> 01:06:16.806
Got that?

808
01:06:18.850 --> 01:06:20.142
For victory!

809
01:06:20.143 --> 01:06:21.019
With honor!

810
01:06:26.983 --> 01:06:30.277
Donghun Academy's pride,
the day of Pythagoras.

811
01:06:30.278 --> 01:06:32.446
I wish you all the best.

812
01:06:34.949 --> 01:06:36.535
Han Ji-woo

813
01:07:39.430 --> 01:07:43.434
2019 Pythagoras Award Competition

814
01:07:47.438 --> 01:07:52.110
Your call cannot be connected...

815
01:07:52.694 --> 01:07:55.196
To Bo-ram: What's going on?
Where are you?

816
01:07:57.866 --> 01:08:01.202
Will you come by 7?

817
01:08:02.536 --> 01:08:03.747
Bo-ram.

818
01:08:04.455 --> 01:08:08.627
I'll tell your teacher that
you're on a trip, so stay home.

819
01:08:09.293 --> 01:08:10.962
It's all for your own good.

820
01:08:16.425 --> 01:08:17.301
Look here.

821
01:08:18.219 --> 01:08:20.263
Where are we going?

822
01:08:20.847 --> 01:08:22.306
You'll find out soon.

823
01:08:34.778 --> 01:08:35.737
Here you go.

824
01:08:36.570 --> 01:08:39.614
Isn't this expensive?

825
01:08:39.615 --> 01:08:43.662
Bo-ram's grandpa's
company sponsors it.

826
01:08:46.122 --> 01:08:47.791
Over there, #7.

827
01:09:11.355 --> 01:09:13.357
What's going on?
Where are you?

828
01:09:14.693 --> 01:09:16.402
She's not coming at all?

829
01:09:17.779 --> 01:09:19.863
She must be in a foul mood
because she ruined the test.

830
01:09:19.864 --> 01:09:22.033
You know she does
whatever she pleases.

831
01:11:07.430 --> 01:11:11.059
It sounded much different
than cell phone, right?

832
01:11:12.435 --> 01:11:13.895
You didn't like it?

833
01:11:15.188 --> 01:11:17.148
I really liked it.

834
01:11:29.327 --> 01:11:30.661
Are you hungry?

835
01:11:32.288 --> 01:11:34.707
Yeah, I'm starving!

836
01:11:41.714 --> 01:11:43.299
Tough life, huh?

837
01:11:44.425 --> 01:11:46.051
It ain't easy living with
a prickly man.

838
01:11:46.052 --> 01:11:49.138
All ready, let's eat.

839
01:11:50.306 --> 01:11:51.140
Here.

840
01:11:52.350 --> 01:11:54.184
Thank you for the meal.

841
01:11:54.185 --> 01:11:56.354
There isn't much to eat...

842
01:12:02.151 --> 01:12:04.319
Wow, it's great.

843
01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:07.073
- Do you like it?
- Yes, absolutely.

844
01:12:14.747 --> 01:12:16.124
Aren't you eating?

845
01:12:17.000 --> 01:12:20.294
Yeah, let's eat.

846
01:12:23.547 --> 01:12:26.425
It's first time seeing you eat.

847
01:12:27.969 --> 01:12:28.844
Is that so?

848
01:13:03.171 --> 01:13:05.048
Thank you for the meal.

849
01:13:05.756 --> 01:13:06.882
Get going.

850
01:13:15.141 --> 01:13:16.309
Good night!

851
01:13:29.530 --> 01:13:30.405
Anon board?

852
01:13:30.406 --> 01:13:31.782
Principal Lee Hye-kyung
What's that?

853
01:13:33.242 --> 01:13:36.203
It's the students' anonymous
Facebook bulletin board.

854
01:13:36.204 --> 01:13:37.580
Pythagoras Problems Leaked

855
01:13:38.289 --> 01:13:40.291
Someone blew the whistle.

856
01:13:42.210 --> 01:13:43.586
What happened?

857
01:13:46.464 --> 01:13:49.924
Students who messed up the test
could be grumbling over it.

858
01:13:49.925 --> 01:13:51.884
Expose and punish them!

859
01:13:51.885 --> 01:13:52.844
Of course.

860
01:13:52.845 --> 01:13:55.180
They really went overboard this time.

861
01:13:55.181 --> 01:13:57.433
Keep a tight lid on them.

862
01:13:58.101 --> 01:14:01.562
This will start a firestorm
if Education Board gets wind of it.

863
01:14:16.452 --> 01:14:18.162
$228, please.

864
01:14:19.372 --> 01:14:21.124
These are $228?

865
01:14:21.874 --> 01:14:23.334
Did you win a lotto?

866
01:14:24.085 --> 01:14:27.630
What's the point of making money?
It's there for us to spend like this.

867
01:14:28.797 --> 01:14:30.798
Thank you, take care!

868
01:14:30.799 --> 01:14:31.925
You as well.

869
01:14:32.676 --> 01:14:35.471
Pardon me, sir.

870
01:14:35.971 --> 01:14:39.392
Aren't you from North Korea...

871
01:14:40.809 --> 01:14:43.854
Right? Dr. Ri Hak-sung?

872
01:14:44.938 --> 01:14:46.190
Ri Hak-sung?

873
01:14:47.691 --> 01:14:48.566
Who...

874
01:14:48.567 --> 01:14:50.860
By golly! So it is you!

875
01:14:50.861 --> 01:14:52.987
It's me, Park Pil-ju!

876
01:14:52.988 --> 01:14:55.448
Kim Il-Sung University,
economics major, sir.

877
01:14:55.449 --> 01:14:58.744
You gave us a math lecture
back in the day.

878
01:14:59.495 --> 01:15:04.374
It's amazing to see North Korea's
math genius in South Korea.

879
01:15:04.375 --> 01:15:07.128
It's an honor, sir.

880
01:15:08.337 --> 01:15:11.882
Wait a minute,
you're Tae-yeon, no?

881
01:15:12.925 --> 01:15:14.593
He is, right?

882
01:15:15.219 --> 01:15:18.931
You're all grown up, incredible.

883
01:15:19.932 --> 01:15:23.018
You take after your father
and look so smart.

884
01:15:24.395 --> 01:15:26.563
I almost forgot.

885
01:15:26.564 --> 01:15:31.902
This is my business card,
please give me a call.

886
01:15:32.570 --> 01:15:34.405
Good to see you,
let's go.

887
01:15:36.782 --> 01:15:38.076
Good, good.

888
01:15:41.995 --> 01:15:44.873
Your real name is Ri Hak-sung?

889
01:15:50.254 --> 01:15:52.715
Is Tae-yeon your son...

890
01:16:10.566 --> 01:16:14.320
I'll free him in Taedong River
when reunification happens.

891
01:16:23.036 --> 01:16:24.830
I love this the most.

892
01:16:26.457 --> 01:16:28.626
I'd love to drink this every day.

893
01:16:31.295 --> 01:16:33.880
- Have this one too.
- No, it's okay.

894
01:16:33.881 --> 01:16:35.633
This is so delicious.

895
01:16:47.978 --> 01:16:51.939
Zeta function has its zeros
only at the negative,

896
01:16:51.940 --> 01:16:55.860
even integers and
complex numbers with real part 1/2.

897
01:16:55.861 --> 01:16:56.904
I see.

898
01:16:57.613 --> 01:17:02.867
Riemann Hypothesis, possibly
the most important mathematics problem

899
01:17:02.868 --> 01:17:08.080
is about to be solved after
160 years by a North Korean?

900
01:17:08.081 --> 01:17:10.792
His name is Ri Hak-sung?

901
01:17:10.793 --> 01:17:14.421
Yes, Ri Hak-sung,
he's a North Korean.

902
01:17:14.422 --> 01:17:18.090
So a North Korean mathematician
proved the Riemann Hypothesis?

903
01:17:18.091 --> 01:17:22.012
It'd be more accurate to say
it's about to be proven.

904
01:17:22.763 --> 01:17:25.014
Other scholars must verify his thesis.

905
01:17:25.015 --> 01:17:27.726
I see, how long
will this process take?

906
01:17:28.977 --> 01:17:29.394
Hey!

907
01:17:29.395 --> 01:17:30.812
I expect it to be about 2 years.

908
01:17:30.813 --> 01:17:32.189
There will be a prize too?

909
01:17:32.190 --> 01:17:36.318
Clay Mathematics Institute
will award $1 million.

910
01:17:36.319 --> 01:17:38.320
On a side note,

911
01:17:38.321 --> 01:17:41.406
I've met Ri when I was young.

912
01:17:41.407 --> 01:17:43.616
It was at a math Olympiad,

913
01:17:43.617 --> 01:17:46.077
so it's been 40 years already.

914
01:17:46.078 --> 01:17:49.206
So that child on the left
is Ri Hak-sung?

915
01:17:49.207 --> 01:17:54.461
Yes, he represented
North Korea at the Olympiad,

916
01:17:54.462 --> 01:17:57.464
and I represented the South.

917
01:17:57.465 --> 01:18:01.760
In the middle is a world renowned
mathematician Paul Erdős.

918
01:18:02.386 --> 01:18:07.266
He called us Epsilons,
and adored us.

919
01:18:07.975 --> 01:18:10.853
He also gifted us fountain pens.

920
01:18:13.397 --> 01:18:14.648
This is it.

921
01:18:25.576 --> 01:18:27.076
Why are you here?

922
01:18:27.077 --> 01:18:28.996
Riemann Hypothesis, right?

923
01:18:33.166 --> 01:18:35.627
Ri Hak-sung,
this is you.

924
01:18:35.628 --> 01:18:38.213
NK Ri Hak-sung Presumably
Proved Riemann Hypothesis

925
01:18:41.467 --> 01:18:42.801
That is so cool...

926
01:18:46.054 --> 01:18:47.014
Look here.

927
01:18:48.056 --> 01:18:53.354
Don't ever mention
Riemann Hypothesis, got that?

928
01:18:56.023 --> 01:18:56.981
Why?

929
01:18:56.982 --> 01:18:59.485
When I tell you not to
do something, then don't!

930
01:19:00.944 --> 01:19:02.154
Don't forget it!

931
01:19:04.407 --> 01:19:05.240
Okay.

932
01:19:15.334 --> 01:19:17.002
Euler Math Research Lab

933
01:19:24.051 --> 01:19:26.844
My reputation is about to be
ruined because of you, asshole!

934
01:19:26.845 --> 01:19:29.972
If this gets out,
we're all dead, so just leave!

935
01:19:29.973 --> 01:19:32.560
Don't do anything
until I call you, got it?!

936
01:19:44.488 --> 01:19:45.280
Goddamn!

937
01:19:46.740 --> 01:19:48.659
Principal

938
01:19:49.452 --> 01:19:50.703
Principal?

939
01:20:07.928 --> 01:20:13.559
So you got the tech lab passcode
from your coding club captain.

940
01:20:22.234 --> 01:20:22.985
Get out.

941
01:20:28.991 --> 01:20:32.495
That's not the test,
I printed a thesis.

942
01:20:33.412 --> 01:20:36.623
I printed a PDF from a site,
and left right away.

943
01:20:36.624 --> 01:20:38.500
Thesis? What thesis?

944
01:20:38.501 --> 01:20:40.711
A mathematics thesis.

945
01:20:46.800 --> 01:20:49.177
I believe you.

946
01:20:50.262 --> 01:20:53.641
You're honest
and loyal to your friends.

947
01:20:54.683 --> 01:20:56.308
But others?

948
01:20:56.309 --> 01:20:58.896
Will they believe you
after seeing this footage?

949
01:20:59.897 --> 01:21:01.564
Especially the parents?

950
01:21:01.565 --> 01:21:03.315
It doesn't matter,
I didn't steal it...

951
01:21:03.316 --> 01:21:05.235
Why doesn't it matter?!

952
01:21:06.862 --> 01:21:11.908
You'll be expelled at the very least
for leaking test material.

953
01:21:11.909 --> 01:21:14.118
A permanent strike on your record.

954
01:21:14.119 --> 01:21:16.288
I really didn't do it, sir.

955
01:21:18.999 --> 01:21:22.126
Your average math score is 40,
but you got 70 this time.

956
01:21:22.127 --> 01:21:24.170
A lowest 9th tier student
suddenly shoots up to top 10%.

957
01:21:24.171 --> 01:21:25.963
How do you explain this?

958
01:21:25.964 --> 01:21:27.465
But that's...

959
01:21:27.466 --> 01:21:30.217
In the end, you'll end up
getting the blame.

960
01:21:30.218 --> 01:21:31.929
Do you understand
what I'm saying?

961
01:21:35.015 --> 01:21:36.058
Let's do it this way.

962
01:21:38.226 --> 01:21:41.979
Transfer out, and this will
blow over quietly.

963
01:21:41.980 --> 01:21:43.355
I already talked to the principal.

964
01:21:43.356 --> 01:21:46.901
What? Why should I...

965
01:21:46.902 --> 01:21:50.322
As I've told you, you can't
do much with your grades here.

966
01:21:50.864 --> 01:21:53.783
Will you apply to college
with your grades?

967
01:21:53.784 --> 01:21:56.078
Or take an entrance exam
on your own?

968
01:21:59.206 --> 01:22:03.126
I'll look for the best school
on your behalf.

969
01:22:03.877 --> 01:22:05.838
- Sir?
- Yes?

970
01:22:07.422 --> 01:22:09.341
I really didn't steal it.

971
01:22:09.883 --> 01:22:14.220
I know, I know you didn't steal,

972
01:22:14.221 --> 01:22:15.930
and I believe you.

973
01:22:15.931 --> 01:22:18.433
But circumstances and evidence
tell a different story.

974
01:22:20.060 --> 01:22:21.018
But...

975
01:22:21.019 --> 01:22:23.605
Under Criminal Law 314,
this is an obstruction of business,

976
01:22:23.606 --> 01:22:26.066
punishable by 5-year imprisonment.

977
01:22:29.027 --> 01:22:32.280
Do you want to go to jail?
Wanna be a convict?

978
01:22:36.910 --> 01:22:38.870
Did Ji-woo really leak it?
Useless pricks are the worst.

979
01:22:38.871 --> 01:22:40.038
He's the legendary welfare recipient.

980
01:22:46.003 --> 01:22:48.296
What a load of bullshit!

981
01:22:48.839 --> 01:22:54.594
Comrade Ri Hak-sung,
who raised our nation's reputation

982
01:22:54.595 --> 01:22:57.805
has been kidnapped
by Southern spies.

983
01:22:57.806 --> 01:23:01.726
This is an underhanded act
that throws cold water

984
01:23:01.727 --> 01:23:05.648
on the pact between two countries
to work towards peace.

985
01:23:06.649 --> 01:23:10.359
Kidnapped? He defected on his own.

986
01:23:10.360 --> 01:23:11.862
He did, indeed.

987
01:23:12.655 --> 01:23:14.656
For the freedom
to study and think.

988
01:23:14.657 --> 01:23:17.700
So? You got something to say?

989
01:23:17.701 --> 01:23:20.203
How did we treat a man
who came here to research?

990
01:23:20.996 --> 01:23:25.499
I'm just thankful
I'm not in charge of this.

991
01:23:25.500 --> 01:23:28.878
NSA agents from America
are coming in tomorrow.

992
01:23:28.879 --> 01:23:31.047
NSA? What the hell for?

993
01:23:31.048 --> 01:23:34.592
The Riemann Hypothesis
is tied to cryptography.

994
01:23:34.593 --> 01:23:37.511
Not only military encryption,
but e-commerce is tied to it,

995
01:23:37.512 --> 01:23:42.099
online banking and shopping,
they'll be cracked wide open.

996
01:23:42.100 --> 01:23:43.309
What will you do?

997
01:23:43.310 --> 01:23:44.311
Isn't it obvious?

998
01:23:45.688 --> 01:23:48.315
Set the record straight,
he came on his accord.

999
01:23:49.149 --> 01:23:51.609
Call the stations and
get us to save us a spot.

1000
01:23:51.610 --> 01:23:54.821
Ri is in no condition to
put on a show on TV.

1001
01:23:54.822 --> 01:23:57.156
Just one appearance.

1002
01:23:57.157 --> 01:24:01.452
One segment is all it takes.

1003
01:24:01.453 --> 01:24:04.038
He lost his son!

1004
01:24:04.039 --> 01:24:05.790
Think about it,
imagine your son died...

1005
01:24:05.791 --> 01:24:07.751
Don't drag my son into this.

1006
01:24:10.963 --> 01:24:16.760
I'm sick of covering for you
all the damn time.

1007
01:24:21.098 --> 01:24:24.810
Bosses upstairs are
just waiting for a reason.

1008
01:24:25.603 --> 01:24:27.980
Pull this off and
get on their good side.

1009
01:24:30.190 --> 01:24:33.818
So a Nobel Prize winner
could come from North Korea?

1010
01:24:33.819 --> 01:24:34.944
That's correct.

1011
01:24:34.945 --> 01:24:37.571
Even though it's North Korea,

1012
01:24:37.572 --> 01:24:40.282
it's still a reason to celebrate
for all Koreans.

1013
01:24:40.283 --> 01:24:42.827
Ri should be invited here
and have an interview.

1014
01:24:42.828 --> 01:24:45.247
International media will swarm in.

1015
01:25:02.806 --> 01:25:03.974
Dr. Ri!

1016
01:25:08.854 --> 01:25:13.275
Beef is best with some blood.

1017
01:25:18.446 --> 01:25:19.364
Dr. Ri.

1018
01:25:20.866 --> 01:25:23.285
Let's head back to our home.

1019
01:25:24.494 --> 01:25:26.955
It's from a reliable source,

1020
01:25:27.455 --> 01:25:29.958
they'll treat you as a scientist.

1021
01:25:31.126 --> 01:25:33.837
Remember the science district
by the Taedong River?

1022
01:25:34.629 --> 01:25:37.131
There's a new high rise there,

1023
01:25:37.132 --> 01:25:40.092
you'll be given the top floor too.

1024
01:25:40.093 --> 01:25:43.013
You'll get the penthouse.

1025
01:25:49.352 --> 01:25:51.313
I'll be frank.

1026
01:25:52.189 --> 01:25:56.735
If I bring you in,
they'll forgive me too.

1027
01:25:57.945 --> 01:25:59.361
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

1028
01:25:59.362 --> 01:26:03.200
Don't be like that,
could you give it a thought?

1029
01:26:04.242 --> 01:26:09.790
You can tell them about
how the South treated you.

1030
01:26:10.708 --> 01:26:14.419
I heard about your son
not too long ago.

1031
01:26:15.378 --> 01:26:18.255
You must be so heartbroken...

1032
01:26:18.256 --> 01:26:19.883
Shut your mouth.

1033
01:26:24.512 --> 01:26:27.015
Do it while they offer
an olive branch.

1034
01:26:27.933 --> 01:26:31.102
When the State Security
takes over the situation,

1035
01:26:31.103 --> 01:26:33.020
who knows what'll happen?

1036
01:26:33.021 --> 01:26:35.107
Bastard...

1037
01:26:39.862 --> 01:26:42.030
2019 Second Semester
Transfer Application Form

1038
01:26:50.622 --> 01:26:52.664
I'm sorry about everything.

1039
01:26:52.665 --> 01:26:56.669
I've been meaning to tell you,
but the agency...

1040
01:26:59.798 --> 01:27:01.966
Instead of surveillance,
think of it as support and protecti...

1041
01:27:01.967 --> 01:27:03.135
Look here.

1042
01:27:04.719 --> 01:27:06.471
Thanks for all you did.

1043
01:27:14.146 --> 01:27:17.315
I kept this from 3 years ago.

1044
01:27:18.108 --> 01:27:22.486
You were going to burn it,
it's still your life's work,

1045
01:27:22.487 --> 01:27:24.823
- you should finish...
- That's enough.

1046
01:27:26.116 --> 01:27:26.950
Sir!

1047
01:27:32.414 --> 01:27:37.044
My son died because of this!

1048
01:27:38.336 --> 01:27:40.881
Do you understand?

1049
01:27:42.424 --> 01:27:46.803
You want me to take this
and put on a show on TV?

1050
01:27:46.804 --> 01:27:48.345
The living must go on living!

1051
01:27:48.346 --> 01:27:49.472
The living?!

1052
01:27:52.017 --> 01:27:53.268
Really?

1053
01:27:55.813 --> 01:27:56.980
Look here.

1054
01:27:58.816 --> 01:28:04.779
After that day,
I already died 3 years ago.

1055
01:28:07.908 --> 01:28:09.450
This won't solve anything...

1056
01:28:09.451 --> 01:28:10.617
Get out!

1057
01:28:10.618 --> 01:28:12.912
My agency is comparable to
State Security in the North!

1058
01:28:12.913 --> 01:28:14.206
Get the hell out!

1059
01:28:46.488 --> 01:28:47.405
Why are you here?

1060
01:28:49.324 --> 01:28:51.409
Are you going somewhere?

1061
01:28:59.626 --> 01:29:00.878
When will you be back?

1062
01:29:02.504 --> 01:29:04.631
You'll come back, right?

1063
01:29:05.840 --> 01:29:06.758
Buzz off.

1064
01:29:07.759 --> 01:29:09.635
What about me?

1065
01:29:09.636 --> 01:29:13.015
Aren't you just happy that
you raised grades for free?

1066
01:29:14.933 --> 01:29:16.977
Is it because of going on TV?

1067
01:29:18.353 --> 01:29:20.354
I overheard...

1068
01:29:20.355 --> 01:29:22.148
If you don't need anything,
get out.

1069
01:29:22.149 --> 01:29:24.316
People don't come around
only if they need something.

1070
01:29:24.317 --> 01:29:26.945
Do I look like someone
you play with when bored?

1071
01:29:28.906 --> 01:29:30.323
Why are you lashing out at me?

1072
01:29:31.491 --> 01:29:33.368
You all suck life out of me...

1073
01:29:34.953 --> 01:29:36.038
Is that...

1074
01:29:36.621 --> 01:29:39.791
how you see me?
That's what I am to you?

1075
01:29:42.044 --> 01:29:45.797
You and I are only after
our own lives.

1076
01:29:55.140 --> 01:29:57.308
You should've
kicked me out from the start!

1077
01:29:57.309 --> 01:30:01.021
Why did you let me
study with you?

1078
01:30:06.443 --> 01:30:09.988
You told me to prove it,
that I shouldn't transfer!

1079
01:30:51.571 --> 01:30:53.947
You didn't steal the test.

1080
01:30:53.948 --> 01:30:56.367
Why are you letting them
frame you?

1081
01:30:56.368 --> 01:30:59.162
Mr. Park can tell them,
that you printed a thesis!

1082
01:31:00.413 --> 01:31:01.873
It's all over.

1083
01:31:10.590 --> 01:31:11.674
Mister?

1084
01:31:12.967 --> 01:31:15.095
Sir, what are you waiting for?

1085
01:31:17.222 --> 01:31:18.890
Where are you going?

1086
01:31:22.060 --> 01:31:23.936
Where is your destination?

1087
01:31:28.441 --> 01:31:29.401
Sir?

1088
01:31:33.280 --> 01:31:36.407
According to our research
into Ri Hak-sung,

1089
01:31:36.408 --> 01:31:41.996
he is the mathematician
mentioned by Prof. Oh Jung-nam.

1090
01:31:42.664 --> 01:31:45.499
He did in fact defect
4 years ago,

1091
01:31:45.500 --> 01:31:48.460
but his current whereabouts
are unknown.

1092
01:31:48.461 --> 01:31:51.088
North Korea has requested
the return of Ri

1093
01:31:51.089 --> 01:31:54.550
through an official statement
announced today.

1094
01:31:54.551 --> 01:32:00.347
It's the first time NK made such request,
accusing SK of kidnapping.

1095
01:32:00.348 --> 01:32:01.515
The government...

1096
01:32:01.516 --> 01:32:03.143
Where is it?
I can't find it.

1097
01:32:07.897 --> 01:32:09.482
I don't have it!

1098
01:32:32.004 --> 01:32:36.926
Dad knows nothing but himself.

1099
01:33:25.933 --> 01:33:29.103
Did you fight again?
What happened?

1100
01:33:33.816 --> 01:33:36.569
My comrades were getting beaten
by South Korean guys,

1101
01:33:37.111 --> 01:33:38.820
was I supposed to just watch?

1102
01:33:38.821 --> 01:33:41.115
Who do you think
I came here for?

1103
01:33:44.536 --> 01:33:46.454
You came here for you!

1104
01:33:47.247 --> 01:33:51.500
Then you should've brought mother,
before she died of tuberculosis!

1105
01:33:51.501 --> 01:33:55.712
You dragged me here
after the lab kicked you out!

1106
01:33:55.713 --> 01:33:58.382
How could you only think like that?

1107
01:33:58.383 --> 01:34:02.594
I brought you here
to show you a better world.

1108
01:34:02.595 --> 01:34:04.054
A better world?

1109
01:34:04.055 --> 01:34:07.974
It must be nice
for a lifelong scholar

1110
01:34:07.975 --> 01:34:11.395
to chop chicken heads,
and work at construction sites!

1111
01:34:11.396 --> 01:34:13.981
Shut your mouth!

1112
01:34:15.400 --> 01:34:19.445
Praise our almighty
Supreme Leader!

1113
01:34:19.446 --> 01:34:22.240
Shut your damn mouth!

1114
01:34:22.824 --> 01:34:26.035
Footstep of our Supreme Leader!

1115
01:34:30.623 --> 01:34:34.794
Use your damn math
and live alone here!

1116
01:35:01.863 --> 01:35:04.906
Return to the shore!
I repeat, return to the shore!

1117
01:35:04.907 --> 01:35:06.534
If you do not comply,
we will open fire!

1118
01:35:07.452 --> 01:35:09.036
Return to the shore!

1119
01:35:09.621 --> 01:35:14.124
A teenager attempting to defect
to the North was shot and killed.

1120
01:35:14.125 --> 01:35:17.461
He did not stop despite
multiple warnings,

1121
01:35:17.462 --> 01:35:20.340
and the border patrol followed
the emergency protocols...

1122
01:36:00.004 --> 01:36:04.301
2019 Second Semester
Transfer Application Form

1123
01:36:30.368 --> 01:36:33.871
17th Donghun Academy
Pythagoras Award Ceremony

1124
01:36:34.497 --> 01:36:36.416
Seoul University

1125
01:36:41.879 --> 01:36:45.800
You did the right thing,
I'll take care of it.

1126
01:36:46.759 --> 01:36:48.928
Don't you worry.

1127
01:36:50.179 --> 01:36:51.055
You may go.

1128
01:36:54.016 --> 01:36:55.477
You did good.

1129
01:37:11.075 --> 01:37:14.161
Bo-ram

1130
01:37:15.204 --> 01:37:17.122
Special Talk: Math and Life

1131
01:37:17.123 --> 01:37:19.791
North Korean Mathematician
Dr. Ri Hak-sung

1132
01:37:19.792 --> 01:37:23.421
Ki-chul, everything's ready here.

1133
01:37:24.964 --> 01:37:26.716
Don't be late.

1134
01:37:31.971 --> 01:37:33.598
Manwoo County

1135
01:37:43.483 --> 01:37:46.819
Sir, where are you?
Ji-woo's transferring!

1136
01:37:48.613 --> 01:37:50.532
At my tutor's class...

1137
01:37:51.449 --> 01:37:53.451
Sir! Sir!

1138
01:37:58.330 --> 01:38:03.877
The 17th Pythagoras Award
ceremony will start soon,

1139
01:38:03.878 --> 01:38:08.299
so please assemble
at the auditorium.

1140
01:38:08.883 --> 01:38:11.468
Attention please.

1141
01:38:11.469 --> 01:38:16.932
The 17th Pythagoras Award
ceremony will start soon,

1142
01:38:16.933 --> 01:38:20.853
so please assemble
at the auditorium.

1143
01:38:37.244 --> 01:38:40.371
Get back in,
why should you leave?

1144
01:38:40.372 --> 01:38:41.248
Stop it.

1145
01:38:43.876 --> 01:38:46.170
Hey, Bo-ram!

1146
01:38:48.590 --> 01:38:49.924
Bo-ram!

1147
01:38:51.593 --> 01:38:52.677
Quiet down!

1148
01:38:56.889 --> 01:39:00.266
Could the homeroom teachers
sit your students?

1149
01:39:00.267 --> 01:39:01.478
Bo-ram, over here.

1150
01:39:02.061 --> 01:39:04.020
Put your cell phones away!

1151
01:39:04.021 --> 01:39:05.356
It's almost time!

1152
01:39:06.065 --> 01:39:08.109
- Who's still standing?!
- Cell phones away.

1153
01:39:09.652 --> 01:39:11.571
Han Ji-woo, sit over there.

1154
01:39:12.530 --> 01:39:13.948
Come on, sit down at once.

1155
01:39:15.032 --> 01:39:16.367
Sit down.

1156
01:39:17.910 --> 01:39:21.080
Why are you still standing?

1157
01:39:33.050 --> 01:39:36.845
You all know our academy's
proud alum,

1158
01:39:36.846 --> 01:39:39.516
and Pythagoras Award's jury,

1159
01:39:40.016 --> 01:39:45.104
let's welcome POSTECH's mathematics
chair professor, Prof. Oh Jung-nam.

1160
01:39:49.859 --> 01:39:51.402
A round of applause!

1161
01:39:57.992 --> 01:40:03.747
Seeing all these bright eyes,
I feel so young.

1162
01:40:03.748 --> 01:40:10.879
I can't start this without mentioning
the great achievement in math recently.

1163
01:40:10.880 --> 01:40:16.844
Mathematicians have struggled to prove
the Riemann Hypothesis for 160 years.

1164
01:40:17.845 --> 01:40:23.016
As you know, a new thesis
has entered verification process.

1165
01:40:23.017 --> 01:40:29.523
The one who will turn this
into the Riemann Theorem is

1166
01:40:30.274 --> 01:40:33.194
found to be a North Korean mathematician.

1167
01:40:35.613 --> 01:40:37.739
- He...
- Isn't that the commie?

1168
01:40:37.740 --> 01:40:40.241
- It's the commie!
- The North Korea mathematician...

1169
01:40:40.242 --> 01:40:41.744
is known as Ri Hak-sung...

1170
01:40:44.371 --> 01:40:49.919
whom I've had the pleasure
of meeting 40 years ago...

1171
01:40:50.670 --> 01:40:55.216
The professor is in the middle
of a speech, please leave.

1172
01:41:13.234 --> 01:41:14.360
No way...

1173
01:41:16.112 --> 01:41:17.864
Ri Hak-sung!

1174
01:41:19.531 --> 01:41:20.783
What's going on?

1175
01:41:21.533 --> 01:41:22.909
It's been so long.

1176
01:41:22.910 --> 01:41:24.745
Ri Hak-sung, I never thought
I'd see you again...

1177
01:41:24.746 --> 01:41:26.873
How long has it been?

1178
01:41:28.415 --> 01:41:30.251
But what brings you here?

1179
01:41:30.918 --> 01:41:35.463
Please pardon my interruption,
but may I say a word?

1180
01:41:35.464 --> 01:41:40.136
Of course! Absolutely!
That's what we want too!

1181
01:41:41.178 --> 01:41:46.643
This is world renowned
Dr. Ri Hak-sung!

1182
01:42:06.287 --> 01:42:07.705
We've all met before.

1183
01:42:10.457 --> 01:42:15.755
I'm the commie officer
just introduced by Prof. Oh.

1184
01:42:20.342 --> 01:42:23.220
The world works in a mysterious way.

1185
01:42:24.221 --> 01:42:29.643
It feels weird standing up here
after patrolling this school for so long.

1186
01:42:31.729 --> 01:42:36.483
Don't worry,
I won't talk math here.

1187
01:42:37.193 --> 01:42:42.614
The reason why I stand here
before you discourteously

1188
01:42:43.449 --> 01:42:45.366
is because of one student.

1189
01:42:45.367 --> 01:42:47.493
Student? Which one?

1190
01:42:47.494 --> 01:42:50.206
He's someone I met here...

1191
01:42:51.540 --> 01:42:53.541
Han Ji-woo.

1192
01:42:53.542 --> 01:42:54.835
Han Ji-woo?

1193
01:42:54.836 --> 01:42:56.628
Is he here?

1194
01:42:57.171 --> 01:42:59.131
If you're present,
raise your hand.

1195
01:43:03.344 --> 01:43:06.263
Yes, there, that's him.

1196
01:43:09.266 --> 01:43:14.063
For the past few months,
I've been studying math with him.

1197
01:43:15.231 --> 01:43:17.565
How could he not tell us?

1198
01:43:17.566 --> 01:43:19.650
As you may know,

1199
01:43:19.651 --> 01:43:25.783
I was told that he is in
a very tough predicament.

1200
01:43:27.451 --> 01:43:31.287
He snuck into the lab
and was framed for something...

1201
01:43:31.288 --> 01:43:33.289
One moment, sir.

1202
01:43:33.290 --> 01:43:36.918
That incident must be
handled by our school.

1203
01:43:36.919 --> 01:43:39.797
I wouldn't know about that.

1204
01:43:42.466 --> 01:43:47.471
What he printed in the lab
isn't the test,

1205
01:43:48.139 --> 01:43:50.141
but this thesis.

1206
01:43:50.724 --> 01:43:51.725
Thesis?

1207
01:43:53.644 --> 01:44:00.359
With my conscience
and honor as a scholar,

1208
01:44:01.360 --> 01:44:06.783
I can tell you for certain,
Han Ji-woo did not steal the test.

1209
01:44:09.660 --> 01:44:14.164
Your conscience and
honor cannot be evidence.

1210
01:44:14.165 --> 01:44:15.416
Euler!

1211
01:44:16.167 --> 01:44:16.918
Pardon?

1212
01:44:17.626 --> 01:44:19.336
Euler's formula.

1213
01:44:21.505 --> 01:44:24.591
It's the most beautiful
formula in the world.

1214
01:44:25.092 --> 01:44:27.052
From what I hear,

1215
01:44:27.053 --> 01:44:32.682
there's a math tutor class
using Euler's name.

1216
01:44:32.683 --> 01:44:33.934
One moment, sir.

1217
01:44:33.935 --> 01:44:36.312
Wait, I'm not done.

1218
01:44:37.229 --> 01:44:38.814
But the thing is,

1219
01:44:38.815 --> 01:44:41.317
the class isn't as beautiful
as its name.

1220
01:44:42.068 --> 01:44:45.487
They are the ones
who supposedly leaked

1221
01:44:46.322 --> 01:44:49.991
the Pythagoras test problems
to its pupils...

1222
01:44:49.992 --> 01:44:51.327
Enough!

1223
01:44:56.040 --> 01:44:57.041
All right.

1224
01:44:58.792 --> 01:45:00.377
Let me ask you something.

1225
01:45:02.839 --> 01:45:10.179
When a teacher frames his pupil
as a thief, is this still a school?

1226
01:45:21.315 --> 01:45:24.110
Can you take responsibility
for what you just said?

1227
01:45:24.986 --> 01:45:29.365
Since we respected you,
do you feel like a teacher?

1228
01:45:31.742 --> 01:45:38.374
Do cats and dogs pretend
to be teachers too nowadays?

1229
01:45:41.710 --> 01:45:42.920
Am I right?

1230
01:45:48.550 --> 01:45:51.136
Blabber whatever you want!

1231
01:45:51.137 --> 01:45:53.180
I'm done with this bullshit...

1232
01:45:55.307 --> 01:45:56.976
Do whatever you want!

1233
01:46:04.483 --> 01:46:06.193
- For real?
- Unbelievable.

1234
01:46:09.780 --> 01:46:14.492
Isn't that proof enough?

1235
01:46:14.493 --> 01:46:16.120
Really? Han Ji-woo?

1236
01:46:20.166 --> 01:46:24.962
I risked my life to defect
to study math properly.

1237
01:46:26.547 --> 01:46:32.177
I found out that my research was
only used to build weapons,

1238
01:46:32.178 --> 01:46:34.931
and left the North
with disillusionment.

1239
01:46:35.847 --> 01:46:43.855
But it's used as a tool to get into
good colleges and good paying jobs.

1240
01:46:44.398 --> 01:46:50.695
Freedom to study, I was mistaken
to think that it existed here.

1241
01:46:50.696 --> 01:46:55.659
In addition, my son...

1242
01:46:57.703 --> 01:46:59.621
followed my greed...

1243
01:47:02.291 --> 01:47:04.126
to the South...

1244
01:47:07.713 --> 01:47:09.548
but ultimately got killed.

1245
01:47:13.135 --> 01:47:22.979
But to keep a promise with
such a pathetic man,

1246
01:47:25.022 --> 01:47:27.524
17-year old Ji-woo...

1247
01:47:28.275 --> 01:47:34.322
he threw away his future.

1248
01:47:34.323 --> 01:47:37.659
Before that student,

1249
01:47:40.079 --> 01:47:42.206
I was just a greedy,

1250
01:47:44.041 --> 01:47:46.210
seemingly pathetic...

1251
01:47:50.839 --> 01:47:53.050
and selfish man...

1252
01:47:58.764 --> 01:48:01.725
who only cared about himself.

1253
01:48:06.855 --> 01:48:09.066
I am truly ashamed.

1254
01:48:16.323 --> 01:48:17.949
Han Ji-woo.

1255
01:48:21.787 --> 01:48:23.080
I'm sorry.

1256
01:48:27.876 --> 01:48:30.087
And thank you.

1257
01:48:43.517 --> 01:48:48.314
We'll start an investigation committee
and get to the bottom of this incident.

1258
01:48:48.814 --> 01:48:53.069
And we will reject
Han Ji-woo's transfer request.

1259
01:48:53.610 --> 01:48:56.655
Could you all return
to your seats?

1260
01:48:57.448 --> 01:48:59.283
Everyone, sit down!

1261
01:49:32.649 --> 01:49:34.526
When will the interview air?

1262
01:49:35.026 --> 01:49:37.529
Give me your phone,
the one I gave you.

1263
01:49:45.662 --> 01:49:46.538
Huh?

1264
01:49:53.420 --> 01:49:54.671
Open it.

1265
01:49:58.509 --> 01:50:03.722
South Koreans have the freedom
of movement and travel.

1266
01:50:04.306 --> 01:50:06.475
It's in the constitution.

1267
01:50:07.058 --> 01:50:12.814
But if you don't return,
we will kidnap you back.

1268
01:50:18.987 --> 01:50:20.197
Will you be okay?

1269
01:50:23.992 --> 01:50:25.661
Don't you worry.

1270
01:50:26.620 --> 01:50:29.080
I won't get shot
like in the North.

1271
01:50:29.706 --> 01:50:32.376
I'll only get fired.

1272
01:50:33.419 --> 01:50:36.380
Maybe I'll continue
to run the junkyard.

1273
01:50:41.343 --> 01:50:42.636
Thank you.

1274
01:51:23.802 --> 01:51:27.013
He wanted me to
give this to you in person.

1275
01:51:29.683 --> 01:51:31.017
What about Mr. Ri?

1276
01:51:31.602 --> 01:51:35.814
We got a hermit mathematician
on our hands.

1277
01:51:36.607 --> 01:51:39.109
He's doing well,
away from everything.

1278
01:51:41.987 --> 01:51:42.946
See you again.

1279
01:51:51.830 --> 01:51:53.832
I understand the fountain pen,

1280
01:51:55.208 --> 01:51:56.167
but what's that?

1281
01:51:57.419 --> 01:51:59.630
First draft of his Riemann thesis.

1282
01:52:01.798 --> 01:52:04.050
Wow, a collector's item!

1283
01:52:04.926 --> 01:52:06.051
Half-half?

1284
01:52:06.052 --> 01:52:07.178
Give it back!

1285
01:52:08.305 --> 01:52:09.556
Piss off.

1286
01:52:11.057 --> 01:52:12.392
Give it!

1287
01:52:12.393 --> 01:52:15.686
You're a yappy one, comrade.

1288
01:52:15.687 --> 01:52:16.979
Stop kidding around
and give it back!

1289
01:52:16.980 --> 01:52:17.980
Buzz off, asshole.

1290
01:52:17.981 --> 01:52:19.566
You'll rip it!

1291
01:52:25.155 --> 01:52:26.864
3 years later

1292
01:52:26.865 --> 01:52:29.409
We are finally approaching
the research institute.

1293
01:52:29.410 --> 01:52:32.996
This is like the holiest site
for all mathematicians.

1294
01:52:33.539 --> 01:52:35.748
Not only as a professor,
but for you students,

1295
01:52:35.749 --> 01:52:39.378
it is an incredible honor
to visit this place!

1296
01:52:39.920 --> 01:52:43.465
We should all be thankful
to Ji-woo for this opportunity.

1297
01:52:52.641 --> 01:52:55.977
Oberwolfach Research Institute
for Mathematics

1298
01:53:40.439 --> 01:53:41.607
You punk.
